    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">There is documentation for labs, if that&#39;s what you&#39;re looking for.  Just ?labs it.  Otherwise, the scales are also uniform with respect to legend naming conventions, in the sense that scale_[aesthetic] always (as I am thinking now) takes as a first argument the title of the legend which it will generate (if indeed it does generate one).  Check Hadley&#39;s webpage at <a href=\"http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792380851320000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1R6M-4NwfeHyyQ9PYhQhLL\">http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/</a> for more info.<div><br></div><div>Hope it helps!</div><div>david.</div><div><div><br></div><div><br><div><div>On Jan 19, 2011, at 10:26 PM, Scott Chamberlain wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>            <div>                <span>I don&#39;t know of any documentation...</span></div><div><span><br></span></div><div><span>Scott</span></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
